 "verses": {
  "bsb|JHN 10:33": {
   "text": "“We are not stoning You for any good work,” said the Jews, “but for blasphemy, because You, who are a man, declare Yourself to be God.”"
  },
  "bsb|JHN 10:34": {
   "text": "Jesus replied, “Is it not written in your Law: ‘I have said you are gods’?"
  },
  "bsb|JHN 10:35": {
   "text": "If he called them gods to whom the word of God came—and the Scripture cannot be broken—"
  },
  "bsb|JHN 10:36": {
   "text": "then what about the One whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world? How then can you accuse Me of blasphemy for stating that I am the Son of God?"
  },
  "bsb|PSA 82:6": {
   "text": "I have said, ‘You are gods; you are all sons of the Most High.’"
  },
